  "created_at": "2026-10-11T15:21:03+00:00",
  "defect": "Four gaps in the original freeze, none affecting any definition or computation of a metric. (1) Nontrivial TRR was used as the headline for the interpretation cases but was never named as the single primary scaling endpoint; seven table rows were all called 'primary'. (2) Cases A-D were stated to be non-exclusive, but not that they are descriptive flags rather than hypothesis-test categories or universal thresholds, and the two adjacent scale steps were not defined with an explicit sign. (3) model_revisions.json was not checksummed and the runner did not verify it. (4) The pre-flight and results-writer scripts were not hashed into any provenance record, and the code gates had no way to honour an amendment.",
  "document": {
    "path": "docs/QWEN_SCALE_ABLATION_AMENDMENT_001.md"
  },
  "inference_existed": false,
  "model_revisions_existed": false,
  "number": 1,
  "outcome_independence": "Created before any FormalCRRC inference with Qwen2.5-7B or Qwen2.5-32B: the amendment script refuses to run if any result, partial result, receipt or run record exists. No 7B or 32B outcome existed to depend on. Four pre-flight submissions had failed on nodes with unusable GPUs before loading any model; they produced no model or scientific output.",
  "preregistration_frozen_at": "2026-10-11T14:55:19+00:00",
